Source files:   main.cc AlbumCreator.cc View.cc PhotoGram.cc MediaFactory.cc Criteria.cc Album.cc Photo.cc Date.cc
Header files:   defs.h Array.h AlbumCreator.h View.h PhotoGram.h MediaFactory.h Criteria.h Album.h Photo.h Date.h
  Data files:   media/phototitles.txt media/photos.txt
  
 Compilation:   make
    Clearing:   make clean
 
   Launching:   ./a4

Both data files are opened by relative path, so a4 must be launched from the
assignment4 directory.

Purpose of classes:

main: Required for executable to run, launches AlbumCreator
AlbumCreator: Control layer, runs the menu loop and uploads the photo list on startup
View: Prints the menus and handles every input prompt
Date: Stores a date using 3 integers, with comparison operators
Array: Template collection with a fixed capacity, used for both Photo* and Album*
Photo: Stores a title, a category, a Date, and ASCII art content
Album: Uses an Array of Photo pointers, with its own title and description
PhotoGram: Stores the master photo list and the albums, creates objects through MediaFactory
MediaFactory: Factory that creates Photos, Albums, and Criteria objects
Criteria: Abstract base class for photo filters. Cat_Criteria filters by category, Date_Criteria filters by date range, and CandD_Criteria inherits from both to filter on category and date range together

Not built into a4:

test.cc: Standalone tests for Date and Array
classa2.py: Helper script that prints a class skeleton for a given class name
